                "senderName": "NWS Reno NV",
                "headline": "Winter Storm Warning issued November 13 at 1:32AM PST until November 14 at 10:00AM PST by NWS Reno NV",
                "description": "* CHANGES...None.\n\n* WHAT...Heavy wet snow. Snow accumulations near 12 inches above 7000\nfeet, with up to 6 inches below 7000 feet. Snow accumulations up to\n20 inches along the crest west of Lake Tahoe. Wind gusts of 70 to\n90 mph over ridges and gusts of 45 to 55 mph for Truckee and Lake\nTahoe communities. Wave heights 2 to 5 feet on Lake Tahoe.\n\n* WHERE...Greater Lake Tahoe Area.\n\n* WHEN...From 10 AM this morning to 10 AM PST Saturday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be very difficult. The hazardous conditions\ncould impact the Friday evening commute. Strong winds and Sierra\ncement snow could cause damage to trees and power lines. Strong\nwinds and rough waves on Lake Tahoe will create hazardous\nconditions for small watercraft.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...A burst of heavy snow is likely with this\nsystem late this afternoon into the evening with snow levels\nfalling to as low as 5500 feet.",
                "instruction": "If you must travel, keep an extra flashlight, food, and water in your\nvehicle in case of an emergency. The latest road conditions for the\nstate you are calling from can be obtained by calling 5 1 1.",
